+# Design - AgentLoop Task Console UI
+
+Task: Build a UI for AgentLoop. The product core is task management, including CRUD, latest task progress, and runtime returns.
+Iteration: 1
+Task artifact directory: "'`.agentloop/tasks/20260519-050850-agentloop-ui-crud-runtime/artifacts/`
+
+## 1. Product Shape
+
+Build **AgentLoop Task Console**: a local, workspace-scoped web UI served by AgentLoop itself.
+
+The first screen is the task operations console, not a landing page. It lets the user scan all tasks, create a task, inspect one task'"'s progress, update safe per-task settings, run lifecycle actions, delete tasks, and read the latest runtime/test output without browsing "'`.agentloop/` manually.
+
+Recommended form:
+
+- Backend: Python standard-library HTTP server or a small optional web server module inside `agentloop/ui.py` and `agentloop/api.py`.
+- Frontend: static HTML/CSS/vanilla JS served from `agentloop/ui_static/`.
+- Storage: existing file-backed `.agentloop/` layout remains the source of truth.
+- Launch command: `python -m agentloop ui [--host 127.0.0.1] [--port 8765]`.
+
+This keeps the UI local-first, install-light, and aligned with the current CLI package. A later iteration can swap the static frontend for React if the control surface grows.
+
+## 2. Goals
+
+- List existing tasks from `.agentloop/tasks/` with id, title, status, phase, iteration progress, updated time, and current-task marker.
+- Create a new task from a raw task request using `workflow.start_task`, so analysis and acceptance artifacts are produced exactly like the CLI.
+- Open a task detail view with goal, lifecycle state, phase statuses, acceptance criteria, artifact previews/links, task config, lifecycle actions, and latest runtime/test output.
+- Update supported per-task settings through existing validation: at minimum `max_iterations` and `test_commands` in `.agentloop/tasks/<id>/config.json`.
+- Delete a task with explicit confirmation, using the same path safety boundaries as `tasks.task_dir` and the CLI delete behavior.
+- Approve, cancel, and run/resume tasks with action availability derived from current status and locks.
+- Show latest persisted progress after lifecycle actions.
+- Show runtime returns from `state.agents` plus stdout/stderr log files under `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/<iteration>/`.
+- Show local test command output from `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/<iteration>/tests/`.
+- Handle missing/malformed files and long logs without crashing.
+
+## 3. Non-Goals
+
+- No hosted deployment, authentication, remote execution, or multi-user collaboration.
+- No replacement of workflow, runtime adapter, task storage, or lock semantics.
+- No direct arbitrary JSON editor for `state.json`.
+- No database.
+- No real-time streaming requirement in the first iteration. Polling and manual refresh are enough.
+
+## 4. Existing Contracts To Reuse
+
+Current code already provides most domain operations:
+
+- Task discovery and IO: `agentloop.tasks.list_task_ids`, `load_task_state`, `save_task_state`, `task_snapshot`, `current_task_id`.
+- Config overlays: `load_task_config`, `effective_config`, `apply_task_config_patch`, `unset_task_config_key`, `clear_task_config`.
+- Lifecycle operations: `workflow.start_task`, `approve_task`, `cancel_task`, `run_task`.
+- Locks: `locks.task_lock`, `LockHeld`.
+- Task path validation: `tasks.task_dir`, `task_state_path`, `task_config_path`.
+- Test logs: `runner.run_test_commands` writes `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/<iteration>/tests/NN-test.log`.
+- Runtime results: `state.agents[]` records role, runtime, command, exit code, timing, stdout/stderr logs, artifacts.
+
+The UI backend should call these Python functions directly instead of shelling out to `python -m agentloop ...`. This avoids parsing CLI output and keeps errors typed as `WorkspaceError` / `LockHeld`.
+
+## 5. Information Architecture
+
+### 5.1 Main Layout
+
+Use a dense operations-console layout:
+
+- Left panel: task list, filters, create button.
+- Center panel: selected task detail and phase timeline.
+- Right/bottom panel: runtime output viewer with role/test tabs.
+
+The first viewport should immediately show task inventory and selected-task status. No hero, marketing copy, or decorative cards.
+
+### 5.2 Task List
+
+Each row shows:
+
+- Current marker.
+- Status badge.
+- Task title.
+- Short task id.
+- Current phase.
+- Iteration `iteration / max_iterations`.
+- Updated time.
+
+Filters:
+
+- Status segmented control: All, Active, Waiting, Running, Done, Blocked, Cancelled.
+- Text search over title/id.
+- Sort: updated desc by default.
+
+Malformed task state rows should still render as `UNKNOWN` with a clear error indicator.
+
+### 5.3 Task Detail
+
+Detail sections:
+
+- Header: title, full task id, status, current phase, iteration, updated time.
+- Lifecycle actions: approve, run/resume, cancel, delete.
+- Goal: raw request and optional structured goal fields.
+- Phase timeline: analysis, alignment, design, implementation, testing, review.
+- Acceptance criteria table: id, required, verification, status, evidence.
+- Artifacts: analysis.md, acceptance.md, acceptance.json, design.md, test-plan.md, review JSONs, final-report.md when present.
+- Config editor: `max_iterations`, `test_commands`.
+- Runtime output: latest role/test returns.
+
+Artifact previews should be read-only. Markdown can be rendered as plain preformatted text in iteration 1 to avoid adding a Markdown dependency.
+
+### 5.4 Runtime Output Viewer
+
+Runtime output is shown as an operational log browser:
+
+- Role tabs: analyst, architect, implementer, tester, reviewer, integrator, tests.
+- Latest iteration selected by default.
+- Optional iteration selector when history exists.
+- Metadata strip: runtime, command, exit code, duration, started/ended time, artifact list.
+- Output panes: stdout, stderr, structured output when available.
+- Test tab: command, exit code, duration, log content for each `NN-test.log`.
+
+Long logs must be bounded server-side and client-side. Default: return the last 64 KiB per log with `truncated: true`, `bytes_returned`, and `bytes_total`.
+
+## 6. Backend Design
+
+### 6.1 Module Split
+
+Add these modules:
+
+- `agentloop/ui.py`: server entry point and static file serving.
+- `agentloop/api.py`: JSON API handlers and task view-model builders.
+- `agentloop/logs.py`: safe log/artifact reading helpers.
+- `agentloop/ui_static/index.html`
+- `agentloop/ui_static/styles.css`
+- `agentloop/ui_static/app.js`
+
+Keep domain logic in existing modules. `api.py` should translate HTTP payloads into calls to `tasks.py` and `workflow.py`.
+
+### 6.2 CLI Command
+
+Add `ui` to `agentloop.cli`:
+
+```text
+python -m agentloop ui [--host 127.0.0.1] [--port 8765] [--open]
+```
+
+Default host must be `127.0.0.1`, not `0.0.0.0`, because this exposes local task state and logs.
+
+### 6.3 API Endpoints
+
+Use JSON endpoints under `/api`.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks`
+
+Returns list rows:
+
+```json
+{
+  "current_task_id": "20260519-050850-agentloop-ui-crud-runtime",
+  "tasks": [
+    {
+      "task_id": "...",
+      "title": "...",
+      "status": "WAITING_FOR_ALIGNMENT",
+      "current_phase": "alignment",
+      "iteration": 0,
+      "max_iterations": 7,
+      "updated_at": "...",
+      "current": true,
+      "error": null
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Implementation notes:
+
+- Iterate `list_task_ids(root)`.
+- Use `load_task_state`; on `WorkspaceError`, return a degraded row.
+- Include `current_task_id(root)`.
+
+#### `POST /api/tasks`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{ "request": "Implement ..." }
+```
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Validate non-empty string.
+- Call `start_task(root, request)`.
+- Return task detail view model.
+
+This satisfies create behavior and preserves existing analysis/acceptance generation.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks/<task_id>`
+
+Returns full detail view model:
+
+```json
+{
+  "state": { "...": "selected safe state fields" },
+  "config": {
+    "override": {},
+    "effective": {}
+  },
+  "actions": {
+    "approve": { "enabled": true, "reason": null },
+    "run": { "enabled": false, "reason": "waiting for alignment approval" },
+    "cancel": { "enabled": true, "reason": null },
+    "delete": { "enabled": true, "reason": null }
+  },
+  "artifacts": [],
+  "runtime": {
+    "iterations": [],
+    "latest_iteration": 0,
+    "agents": [],
+    "tests": []
+  },
+  "errors": []
+}
+```
+
+Do not return arbitrary files outside task artifacts/runs.
+
+#### `PATCH /api/tasks/<task_id>/config`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{
+  "max_iterations": 5,
+  "test_commands": ["python -m unittest discover -s tests"]
+}
+```
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Acquire `task_lock(root, task_id, blocking=False)` to avoid editing during runs.
+- Apply supported keys through `apply_task_config_patch`.
+- For multi-key updates, validate all keys before saving. If existing helper only patches one dotted key at a time, add an API-level transaction that loads override, merges allowed keys, reuses validation, then saves once.
+- Return updated raw/effective config.
+
+Minimum supported fields are `max_iterations` and `test_commands`. Runtime role overrides can be exposed later.
+
+#### `DELETE /api/tasks/<task_id>`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{ "confirm": "<task_id>" }
+```
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Require exact confirmation match.
+- Refuse delete if task lock is held.
+- Resolve target with `task_dir(root, task_id)` and verify it is under `.agentloop/tasks/`.
+- Remove directory.
+- If deleted task is current, reset current state as CLI does.
+- Return `{ "deleted": true }`.
+
+This mirrors `cmd_tasks_delete` safety boundaries.
+
+#### `POST /api/tasks/<task_id>/approve`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{ "by": "requester" }
+```
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Acquire task lock.
+- Call `approve_task(root, approved_by=..., task_id=task_id)`.
+- Return refreshed detail.
+
+#### `POST /api/tasks/<task_id>/cancel`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{ "by": "requester" }
+```
+
+Behavior:
+
+- Acquire task lock.
+- Call `cancel_task(root, cancelled_by=..., task_id=task_id)`.
+- Return refreshed detail.
+
+#### `POST /api/tasks/<task_id>/run`
+
+Payload:
+
+```json
+{ "wait": false }
+```
+
+Iteration 1 can run synchronously:
+
+- Acquire task lock with `blocking=wait`.
+- Call `run_task(root, task_id=task_id)`.
+- Return refreshed detail when complete.
+- If lock is held, return HTTP 409 with lock message.
+
+Risk: long requests can block the browser. The first UI should show a modal/progress state and poll `/api/tasks/<id>` after the request completes or fails. A later iteration can introduce background jobs.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks/<task_id>/artifacts/<name>`
+
+Returns bounded artifact content for known files in `.agentloop/tasks/<task_id>/artifacts/`.
+
+Rules:
+
+- Normalize `name` to a basename or a safe relative path under the artifact directory.
+- Reject `..`, absolute paths, and path separators when not explicitly supported.
+- Return content as UTF-8 with replacement on decode errors.
+- Bound large files with the same 64 KiB default.
+
+#### `GET /api/tasks/<task_id>/logs?iteration=latest&role=reviewer&type=stdout`
+
+Optional endpoint if logs are not embedded in detail. It returns one bounded log payload.
+
+## 7. View-Model Builders
+
+Add pure functions in `agentloop/api.py` for testability:
+
+- `build_task_list(root) -> dict`
+- `build_task_detail(root, task_id) -> dict`
+- `available_actions(state, lock_info=None) -> dict`
+- `list_task_artifacts(root, task_id) -> list[dict]`
+- `latest_runtime_summary(root, state) -> dict`
+
+### 7.1 Action Availability
+
+Rules:
+
+- Approve enabled only when `status == WAITING_FOR_ALIGNMENT`.
+- Run enabled only when `status in {READY_TO_START, DESIGNING}`.
+- Cancel enabled unless `status in {CREATED, DONE, CANCELLED}`.
+- Delete enabled when no lock is held; still require confirmation.
+- Config update enabled when no lock is held and task is not deleted/malformed.
+
+Disabled actions must include a short reason so the UI can explain the state without guessing.
+
+### 7.2 Latest Runtime Summary
+
+Derive latest iteration from:
+
+- `state.iteration` as primary.
+- `state.agents[].iteration` if present.
+- Existing run directories under `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/` as fallback.
+
+For each agent result:
+
+- Include role, runtime, command, exit code, started_at, ended_at, duration when present.
+- Include artifact refs.
+- Resolve `stdout_log` and `stderr_log` only if path is under workspace root.
+- Read bounded log content.
+- Surface missing logs as `{ "missing": true }`, not as an exception.
+
+For tests:
+
+- Prefer test results embedded in latest review JSON'"'s "'`test_results`.
+- Also scan `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/<iteration>/tests/*.log` and attach content.
+- If commands are configured but no test logs exist, show an empty state: `No test output for this iteration`.
+
+## 8. Frontend Design
+
+### 8.1 Visual Direction
+
+Use a quiet, utilitarian operations-console style:
+
+- Dense but readable tables.
+- Neutral background with status accents.
+- Small icons for actions where available; if avoiding dependencies, use clear text buttons for command actions.
+- No nested cards. Use panels, dividers, tabs, and tables.
+- Stable dimensions for task rows, action toolbar, phase timeline, and log viewer.
+- Monospace for ids/logs; regular sans-serif for labels.
+
+Status accents:
+
+- `WAITING_FOR_ALIGNMENT` / `WAITING_FOR_HUMAN`: amber.
+- `READY_TO_START`: blue.
+- `DESIGNING`, `IMPLEMENTING_AND_TESTING`, `REVIEWING`: cyan.
+- `DONE`: green.
+- `BLOCKED`: red.
+- `CANCELLED`: gray.
+- `UNKNOWN`: red outline.
+
+Avoid a one-color palette by using neutral surface colors plus limited semantic accents.
+
+### 8.2 Interaction Details
+
+Create task:
+
+- Button opens a compact drawer/dialog with a textarea for raw request.
+- Submit calls `POST /api/tasks`.
+- On success, select the new task and show its analysis/acceptance artifacts.
+
+Update config:
+
+- `max_iterations`: numeric input, min 1.
+- `test_commands`: editable list with add/remove rows.
+- Save button disabled until changed.
+- Server validation errors are shown inline.
+
+Delete:
+
+- Confirmation dialog requires typing the full task id.
+- After delete, refresh list and select the next available task.
+
+Lifecycle:
+
+- Approve, Run, Cancel are in a fixed action bar in the detail header.
+- Invalid actions render disabled with tooltip/title reason.
+- Run shows a blocking progress state for synchronous v1; task list/detail refresh after completion.
+
+Runtime output:
+
+- Tabs do not resize the surrounding layout.
+- Logs use `white-space: pre-wrap`, bounded height, and scroll.
+- Show `truncated` indicator with byte counts when content is clipped.
+
+Refresh:
+
+- Poll selected task every 2-5 seconds while a lifecycle action is in progress.
+- Manual refresh button reloads list and detail.
+
+## 9. Error Handling
+
+API error shape:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "code": "workspace_error",
+    "message": "Cannot run while status is WAITING_FOR_ALIGNMENT"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+HTTP status mapping:
+
+- 400: invalid request payload or unsupported config key.
+- 404: task/artifact/log not found.
+- 409: task lock held or invalid lifecycle state.
+- 500: unexpected server error with a generic message and details logged to stderr.
+
+UI behavior:
+
+- Keep the user on the same task after errors.
+- Show stale data with an error banner rather than blanking the page.
+- Malformed task files render in list/detail as recoverable errors.
+
+## 10. Security And Safety
+
+- Bind to `127.0.0.1` by default.
+- Do not serve arbitrary workspace files.
+- Artifact/log endpoints must enforce resolved paths stay inside the expected task artifact/run directory.
+- Delete requires explicit typed confirmation.
+- Config editor only supports allowlisted keys.
+- Lifecycle operations use existing locks.
+- No shell command execution from user-provided UI fields except existing `test_commands`, which AgentLoop already supports as task configuration. The UI should label test commands as local shell commands.
+
+## 11. Implementation Plan
+
+### Phase 1 - Read-Only Console
+
+- Add `ui` command and local static server.
+- Implement `GET /api/tasks` and `GET /api/tasks/<id>`.
+- Build task list, detail summary, phase timeline, artifact list, and bounded runtime/test log display.
+- Add tests for view-model builders using temp workspaces.
+
+Exit criteria: existing tasks are visible and selected task shows progress/artifacts/latest logs.
+
+### Phase 2 - CRUD
+
+- Add create task dialog wired to `start_task`.
+- Add config update for `max_iterations` and `test_commands`.
+- Add delete with typed confirmation.
+- Add API tests for create/update/delete in temp workspaces.
+
+Exit criteria: AC-2, AC-4, AC-5 pass through API tests and browser smoke.
+
+### Phase 3 - Lifecycle Actions
+
+- Add approve/cancel/run endpoints and buttons.
+- Enforce action availability and lock handling.
+- Refresh task detail after mutations.
+- Add tests for status-specific actions and state transitions.
+
+Exit criteria: approve/run/cancel are available only when valid and persisted state updates appear in UI.
+
+### Phase 4 - Runtime Output Polish
+
+- Improve role/test tab grouping.
+- Add iteration selector.
+- Add missing-log and truncated-log states.
+- Add malformed/missing file tests.
+
+Exit criteria: latest runtime and test returns satisfy AC-8, AC-9, AC-10.
+
+## 12. Testing Strategy
+
+Automated tests should avoid the user'"'s real "'`.agentloop` data.
+
+Add tests in `tests/test_ui_api.py`:
+
+- Seed temp workspace with multiple task directories; assert task list fields and current marker.
+- Seed valid detail state with artifacts; assert detail view includes phase statuses, acceptance criteria, artifact metadata.
+- Seed malformed `state.json`; assert list still returns an `UNKNOWN` row with error.
+- Create task through API handler; assert `state.json`, `analysis.md`, `acceptance.md`, `acceptance.json` exist.
+- Patch config; assert `.agentloop/tasks/<id>/config.json` contains `max_iterations` and `test_commands`, and effective config reflects them.
+- Delete task; assert directory removed and current state reset when needed.
+- Approve/cancel actions; assert valid transitions and invalid states return errors.
+- Seed `state.agents` with stdout/stderr logs; assert bounded content and metadata returned.
+- Seed test logs under `.agentloop/runs/<task_id>/<iteration>/tests/`; assert command/test log output is visible.
+- Seed a large log; assert truncation metadata.
+
+Manual/browser smoke:
+
+- Start server with `python -m agentloop ui --port 8765`.
+- Open `http://127.0.0.1:8765`.
+- Verify first screen is task console.
+- Create a task, approve it, update config, run with manual runtime, inspect logs, delete a test task.
+
+## 13. Acceptance Criteria Mapping
+
+- AC-1: `GET /api/tasks` plus task list UI.
+- AC-2: `POST /api/tasks` calling `start_task`.
+- AC-3: `GET /api/tasks/<id>` detail sections.
+- AC-4: `PATCH /api/tasks/<id>/config` using existing validation.
+- AC-5: `DELETE /api/tasks/<id>` with typed confirmation and safe path resolution.
+- AC-6: action availability model plus approve/cancel/run endpoints.
+- AC-7: refreshed detail after lifecycle mutations and polling while running.
+- AC-8: `latest_runtime_summary` from `state.agents` and role logs.
+- AC-9: test log scan and review `test_results` display.
+- AC-10: degraded rows, missing-log states, bounded log reads, malformed-file tests.
+- AC-11: temp-workspace API/view-model tests.
+- AC-12: console-first layout with task CRUD, lifecycle controls, progress, and runtime output.
+
+## 14. Open Questions For Implementation
+
+- Whether to keep v1 run synchronous or immediately add a background job table. Recommendation: synchronous v1, because existing `run_task` is synchronous and this avoids inventing a second execution state model.
+- Whether to expose role runtime overrides in the first config editor. Recommendation: defer unless needed; ship `max_iterations` and `test_commands` first to satisfy the core CRUD/config requirement.
+- Whether artifact preview should render Markdown. Recommendation: plain text first; Markdown rendering can be added client-side later.
+- Whether batch operations belong in the first UI. Recommendation: list filtering can prepare for batch, but defer batch mutation controls until single-task actions are reliable.
+
